/// A function called under a case other than its declaration.
///
/// A function name is an ordinary binding in the enclosing environment, so this
/// is the same lookup as a variable's -- but a call is resolved before the
/// callee is known to be callable, and the diagnostic says 'variable' rather
/// than 'function', which is worth keeping visible.
///
/// Fails with: Undefined variable 'ANSWER'.
///
function Answer () : Integer;
begin
    Exit 42;
end

test 'A function resolves through any spelling of its name';
begin
    AssertEqual (42, ANSWER ());
end
